}}}}}\pard\sb0\sl-240{\bkmkstart Pg2}{\bkmkend Pg2}\par\pard\ql \li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\ri1251\sb14\sl-264\slmult0\fi0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21 The \ul0\nosupersub\cf4\f5\fs21 Internet\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  is a global system of interconnected \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs21 computer networks\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  that use the standard \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs21 Internet \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 Protocol Suite\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  (TCP/IP) to serve billions of users worldwide. It is a \ul0\nosupersub\cf6\f7\fs21 network of networks\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  that consists of \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 millions of private, public, academic, business, and government networks of local to global scope that \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 are linked by a broad array of electronic and optical networking technologies. The Internet carries a vast \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 array of \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs21 information\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  resources and services, most notably the inter-linked \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs21 hypertext\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  documents of the \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs21 World Wide Web\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  (WWW) and the infrastructure to support \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs21 electronic mail\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21 . \par\pard\ql \li1401\ri1220\sb260\sl-260\slmult0\fi0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 An \ul0\nosupersub\cf4\f5\fs21 intranet\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  is a private \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs21 computer network\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  that uses \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs21 Internet Protocol\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21  technologies to securely share \line \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 any part of an organization's information or operational systems within that organization. The term is \line \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 used in contrast to \ul0\nosupersub\cf6\f7\fs21 internet\ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21 , a network between organizations, and instead refers to a network within an \line \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 organization. \par\pard\ql \li1588\sb279\sl-310\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf2\f3\fs27 Q. Define the following terms: \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb31\sl-310\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 A) Heuristic \par\pard\qj \li1401\ri2969\sb12\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21 A procedure that usually, but not always, works or that gives nearly the right answer \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Rule of thumb learned through trial & error \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb16\sl-241\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Common sense lesson drawn from experience \par\pard\ql \li1401\ri3096\sb4\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Qualitative principle, guideline, general judgment \line \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Natural language description of experience \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb299\sl-310\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf2\f3\fs27 B) System \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb28\sl-241\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21 System \par\pard\qj \li1401\ri3106\sb4\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 A collection of elements which working together produces a result not achieved by \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 the things alone \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb33\sl-264\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf8\f9\fs23 C) System architecture \par\pard\ql \li1401\ri4368\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21 System Architecture \line \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 The structure \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb1\sl-235\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 (in terms of components, connections, constraints) of a product or a process \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb0\sl-264\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb38\sl-264\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf8\f9\fs23 D) Analysis of Algorithm \par\pard\qj \li1401\ri2763\sb0\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21 Analysis in the context of algorithms is concerned with predicting the resources that re \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 requires: \par\pard\ql \li1401\ri4378\sb0\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Computational time \line \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Memory \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb16\sl-241\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Bandwidth \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb40\sl-241\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Logic functions \par\pard\qj \li1401\ri1242\sb4\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 However, Time - generally measured in terms of the number of steps required to execute an algorithm -\line \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 is the resource of most interest \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb16\sl-241\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 By analyzing several candidate algorithms, the most efficient one(s) can be identified. \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb0\sl-310\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1401\sb253\sl-310\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs27 Q.  Write a note on the following (4+6) \par\pard\ql \li1401\sb29\sl-264\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf8\f9\fs23 Two popular review methods \par\pard\qj \li2102\ri2287\sb0\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf3\f4\fs21 1. Give the problem statement, design, and code (that includes all assumptions) to a \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 peer, and ask him/her to see if things have been done properly \par\pard\sect\sectd\fs24\paperw11900\paperh16840{\shp
